From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:20:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 144/151] Find: the count and Find next take empty matches, as
 in Notepad++

Notepad++ counts `^` once per line and Find next steps from line to
line. The count, Find next/previous over lines and inside "In
selection" now take empty matches as Replace all does: not overlapping,
and an empty match right after the previous match is skipped. Find next
from an empty match at the cursor moves on, and that match shows its
number ("2 of 3"). The highlights still skip empty matches: there is
nothing to draw.

The Replace all test for `^\s+` and `\s+$` now expects the blank lines
to go too, after the previous commit sent `\s` over lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

